cuju reimplements Google Research Football (https://github.com/google-research/football),
Copyright 2019 Google LLC, Apache License 2.0. Its engine descends from Gameplay Football by
Bastiaan Konings Schuiling, dedicated to the public domain. Files that carry a Google line were
rewritten from that code by the cuju Authors in 2026. animations.bin and the asset bundles are
derived from the data and scenarios of Google Research Football.
cuju is not affiliated with or endorsed by Google.

include/cuju/libm ports math functions of the GNU C Library 2.39 (LGPL 2.1 or later). Where Arm
Optimized Routines v21.02 (MIT, Copyright Arm Limited) or FreeBSD's msun (the notice of Sun
Microsystems, Inc.) holds the same code, the port is taken from there under that license. Each file
reproduces its upstream notices and names its license. The libraries of cuju compile these
functions in, and the complete source of each release is published with it.

The world RNG follows Boost.Random (Boost Software License 1.0). The episode seeds follow MT19937
by Makoto Matsumoto and Takuji Nishimura (BSD-3-Clause), as CPython's random module uses it.

